The page is styled as **The Ledger of the Common Bill** — an invoice that bills you 25 limericks about people named Bill. It opens with a stamped, barcode-stamped invoice header (scramble-decoded title, thumping "APPROVED" stamp), then a sticky table-of-contents rail that tracks your progress through all 25 items, each set as a ledger entry with portrait, annotation, and rubber stamp. Mid-ledger there's an office memo auditing every sense of the word "bill," plus terms of the ledger where **Jurgen** disputes item 04 and the **economist** (item 03) bills the Office for auditing the meter.

